   "source": [
    "# 🌿 Paraclea Custom Voice Training\n",
    "\n",
    "**What this notebook does:** Trains a custom AI voice from any public-domain audiobook using the BMO workflow. By the end, you'll have a `paraclea.onnx` voice model that can speak any text you type.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The pipeline in one sentence:** Chop an audiobook into clips → transcribe what was said → teach a neural network to speak new text in that voice.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why this works:** We start with a pre-trained English voice (`en_US-lessac-medium`) that already knows how to speak. Your audiobook clips only teach it a *new voice timbre* — like a voice actor learning an accent. This is called **fine-tuning** and is much faster than training from scratch.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Requirements:** Set Runtime → Change runtime type → GPU (T4 is free and sufficient). Training takes ~4–6 hours.\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
